/* ============================================================================
 * CONJECTURE (NOT a real model result) -- R3-note: sign(l1) is not the LOS test
 * ============================================================================
 * RETIRED to conjecture status per formalization review.  The previous proved
 * "R3note_l1_not_criterion.kyx" (2 entries) was judged VACUOUS: it only showed two
 * INDEPENDENT reals can be chosen (l1=-1, M=2, Vg=1), not that the LCL model has a
 * parameter point where l1(p)<0 AND a sync equilibrium exists AND the system still
 * globally loses sync.  That is a model-level statement, a whole layer harder.
 *
 * The reviewer offered a concrete witness Kp_pll=0.50, Ki_pll=400.  HONEST OUTCOME:
 * in our weak-grid Hopf pipeline (formalization/numerical/sweep.py) that point gives
 * l1 = +1.4e-6 (POSITIVE), not negative -- we could NOT reproduce l1<0 there.  Either
 * the witness lives in a different model/convention, or our l1 normalization differs.
 * We do NOT fake agreement.  Therefore R3-note is OPEN:
 *
 * GENUINE TARGET (open): exhibit an OPEN set U in LCL parameter space with, for all p in U,
 *   (i)   l1(p) < 0           (locally supercritical, 'safe' by the Bautin reading);
 *   (ii)  |M(p)| < Vg         (a synchronization equilibrium EXISTS, R2-inside);
 *   (iii) the operating equilibrium has NO positive-measure forward-invariant
 *         neighborhood with |theta_e - theta_e*| < pi/2  (global LOS under finite kick).
 * Needs: a reproducible l1(p)<0 region, a basin/kick time-domain certificate, and a
 * continuity/open-set argument -- none of which we currently have.
 *
 * Problem-only CONJECTURE placeholder (no Tactic). */

ArchiveEntry "conjecture_R3note: l1<0, sync exists, yet global LOS coexist on an open LCL set (OPEN; no tactic)"

Problem
  \forall l1 \forall M \forall Vg
  ( l1 < 0 & Vg > 0 & M^2 < Vg^2  ->  M^2 < Vg^2 )
End.

End.
